  NESTED-REPO STRUCTURE — turn a nested repo into parent-tracked content (and back):
  flatten | fl             Nested repo -> parent content; DISPOSES of its live .git.
                           3 equal modes: --merge (kept/deleted) / --sidecar (.git.real,
                           history kept) / --zip (archived)
  unflatten | unfl         Reverse of flatten — rebuild a live .git (--merge/--sidecar/--zip; auto-detects)
  shadow | sh              KEEP the nested .git live (IDE works) AND make the parent
                           track its files too — a content-mirror
  unshadow | unsh          Reverse of shadow — parent stops tracking; .git stays live

  sync | syn               Composite: sm → pull → mc (settle the tree in one shot)
  remote | rem             List / audit git remotes across the tree (--check for warnings)
  audit                    Read-only health checks (--claude and/or --sidecar)
  repair                   Fix sidecar setup problems (--sidecar; analyze, 'go' to apply)
  help                     Show this help

Global options:
  -V, --verbose            Verbosity level 1
  -VV, --very-verbose      Verbosity level 2
  -D, --debug              Debug level 1  (implies -V)
  -DD, --deep-dbg          Debug level 2  (implies -VV; enables set -x)
  -R, --recursive          Force-recurse. For 'mc'/'sm': walk the full
                           submodule tree. For 'st': force discovery of
                           unregistered nested repos in a FOREIGN scope
                           (one outside GIT_REPOS) — managed scopes
                           recurse by default, -R is a no-op there.
  --config <FILE>          Use specific config file
  --create-config          Write default config to first writable location
  --run-tests [PATTERN]    Run the built-in self-test suite (builds real
