    # 'git add' for the parent. This is the headline case: one child
    # has real commits, the other has NONE at all (an unborn HEAD) —
    # which previously made the ENTIRE 'git add' fail fatally
    # ("does not have a commit checked out"), taking down every other
    # path in the same batch with it. Both children must come out the
    # other side fully intact and untouched.
