    # out fails FATALLY ("does not have a commit checked out"), so the
    # direct sidecar->merge path staged nothing and committed nothing (or
    # only partially) — yet reported success, AFTER already deleting
    # .git.real. Fixed by shielding nested repos before the add (restored
    # after), plus honest failure handling. Here 'kid' (a sidecar)
    # contains embok (embedded repo WITH a commit) and embempty (embedded
    # repo with NO commit — the fatal trigger). The merge must commit
    # .git.merged, and leave BOTH nested repos byte-identical.
